The `36cd...` value is the expected `app-version` response header hash/checksum — used to detect app version changes (cache invalidation). Not a secret.

The bundle reveals an internal mechanism: the app compares the `app-version` response header against this hash and triggers a refresh when it differs. This is an app-internal cache invalidation design, not a vulnerability.

