STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] app.alfaview.com/graphql: `GET /graphql` + `X-Apollo-Operation-Name` header satisfies Apollo CSRF preflight and executes anonymous queries read-only — recovered 9 reply types via validation-error oracle (`GetPasscodeReply`, `ListLinksReply`, `SearchCompaniesReply`→field `companies`, `FetchUserPermissionsReply`→arg `userId:String!`, `GenerateFileDownloadURLReply`→arg `roomId:String!`, `CreateMagicTokenReply`, `TokenAuthenticateReply`→arg `magicToken:String!`, `GuestAuthenticateReply`, `GuestJoinReply`). Mutations over GET rejected `405` ("GET requests only support query operations").
- [NEW] GraphQL resolver auth re-tested anonymously: `searchCompanies`, `listAllUserIds`, `getPasscode` all → `UNAUTHENTICATED` (enforced); `listIdentityProviders` → open `{"providers":[]}`; `listComponents` → anonymous `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR`. Sensitive admin resolvers are gated — per-resolver-auth is stricter than the previous session's sample suggested.
- [NEW] REST OpenAPI reconfirmed live (GET /v2/docs/openapi.json, 44 endpoints): `AuthenticateGuestLinkRequestBody` requires `{companyId,roomId,accessKey}` (accessKey untyped string); `GroupLink`/`GuestLink` expose `dialInCode` + `externalId`(min 32) secrets; `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/passcode` GET returns passcode to any authed caller with permission.
- [NEW] Bundle op-AST parse (1.09MB, re-fetched GET) confirms `guestJoin(userId,companyId,roomId,displayName)` and `guestAuthenticate(userId,companyId,roomId)` carry NO accessKey arg; admin ops `listRoomLinks`/`listCompanyLinks` return `accessKey`+`guestId`+`joinLink`+`dialInCode`.
- [CHANGED] Guest "accessKey-bypass" reframed: `joinLink` is itself the shared secret carrier — the web join flow is triple-based by design and REST `accessKey` is the dial-in/API secret. Triple-only guestAuth is design, not divergence; the residual risk is guest-authz (lifecycle/cross-tenant), not secret bypass.

